<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nicolaus von Jeroschin</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">died c. 1341</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> · Also known as Nikolaus von Jeroschin</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Nicolaus von Jeroschin was a priest of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/teutonic-order">Teutonic Order</a> and a Middle High German poet in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-prussia">Prussia</a>. In the 1330s he translated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peter-of-dusburg">Peter of Dusburg</a>'s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin">Latin</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chronicon-terrae-prussiae">Chronicle of the Prussian Land</a> into German verse as the Kronike von Pruzinlant, adding some material of his own. His work is an important example of the literature produced within the Order.</p></div>
